From 38d8a6471e99a3805a0cc8cf8e298bbcc0daf6c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 15:55:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CR-012-Nov - Code lists stored per specialty; PDx POA and
 exempt rule in review

The coding screen sent a blank E/M form with every chart and the result
writer keyed E/M on its presence, so every IP, OP and ED Single Path result
stored empty SDx and CPT lists. E/M is now decided by specialty, the screen
sends the form only for E/M and ED Profee, and lists stored empty are
repaired on read from the coder's draft and the answer key - for the review,
the auditor's observed plantings and Specificity Drops. The review shows the
principal diagnosis POA and marks POA-exempt codes as not graded.

